message: "If you use this software or the study's measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "Authored-Plan Agents: Reference Implementation and Measurement Study of an Architectural Pattern for LLM Agent Platforms"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Senhor Ferreira"
    given-names: "Estefano"
    email: "estefano.senhor@gmail.com"
date-released: "2026-07-27"
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - agent orchestration
  - architectural patterns
  - saga compensation
  - structured output
  - false success
abstract: >
  Reference implementation of an architectural pattern for LLM agent platforms
  in which non-determinism is confined to selection and generation, never to
  sequence. Includes a restriction-enforcing test suite and three cycles of
  real-model measurement: false success over real persistence (100% silent
  corruption -> 0 with decoding-level structured output plus an architectural
  contract guard), compensation over persisted state including failure of the
  compensation itself, and selection accuracy at catalog scale (ambiguity as a
  ~75% floor rather than a catalog-size slope; 100% out-of-catalog refusal).
